<h2 class="bde-heading-506-117 bde-heading">
How Much Is Brandon Williams’s Contract Worth?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-118 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-141 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-154 bde-f-text">
<p>Williams signed with Golden State on August 26, 2026, one year at the veteran minimum of <strong>$2.63m</strong>, with nothing guaranteed.</p>
<p>A contract with no guarantee means the club owes him nothing if it waives him before the league’s January deadline. Signing in late August, after most rosters are settled, is how players in his position get their chance.</p>

</div><div class="bde-shortcode-506-191 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="proportions">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/_ported/08ba6176394a.css">
<h3>Brandon Williams’s Salary As a Percentage of Cap and Payroll</h3><div class="nf-proportion-layout"><div class="nf-proportions"><figure><div class="nf-donut" role="img" aria-label="1.59% of Salary Cap" style="--share:1.5916653027079%"><span>1.59%<small class="nf-change nf-change-none" title="Previous-season comparison unavailable">—</small></span></div><figcaption>Salary Cap</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="nf-donut" role="img" aria-label="1.19% of Team Payroll" style="--share:1.1889357193045%"><span>1.19%<small class="nf-change nf-change-none" title="Previous-season comparison unavailable">—</small></span></div><figcaption>Team Payroll</figcaption></figure></div><div class="nf-proportion-copy"><p>Williams's <strong>$2.63m</strong> takes up <strong>1.59%</strong> of the <strong>$164.96m</strong> salary cap and <strong>1.19%</strong> of Golden State's <strong>$220.84m</strong> payroll. The cap is a benchmark, and clubs are allowed to spend past it under certain rules.</p><p><a href="https://www.nba.com/news/free-agency-explained">How Do Salary Caps Work in the NBA?</a></p></div></div><script src="/_ported/8334868131c3.js" is:inline></script>
