<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Do the Warriors Pay Brandon Williams $2.63m?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Williams is on a non-guaranteed minimum because he can score off the bench and hasn’t yet held a rotation place long enough for a club to commit.</p>
<ul>
<li>He creates his own shot, which is a rare thing in a player available at this price.</li>
<li>He went undrafted out of Arizona in 2021, so his career started with a ten-day contract rather than four guaranteed years.</li>
<li>He’s 6’1″, and guards that size have to score efficiently to justify what they give up defensively.</li>
<li>He’s spent three of five seasons on two-way contracts, so he’s never built the service time that improves a player’s negotiating position.</li>
<li>Nothing in this contract is guaranteed, which means the club is paying for a look at him rather than for a season.</li>
</ul>
<p>Surviving to January would give him the first fully paid season of his career.</p>

</div><div class="bde-shortcode-506-159 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="why">
