<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/brandon-williams/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/brandon-williams/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Brandon Williams’s Salary With the Warriors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Williams earns $2.63m in 2026-27, up from $2.27m last season. He’s fourteenth on the Golden State payroll, level with Dalen Terry on the same figure and the same structure. None of it is guaranteed. His career earnings come to about $4.90m across five seasons, and three of those produced no published salary. The figure is 1.19% of Golden State’s $220.84m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Brandon Williams Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Williams has no guaranteed money, so the immediate question is whether he's on the roster past the January deadline when salaries become fully protected. Clearing that date would take him to free agency in the summer of 2027 at 27 with a full season behind him."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Brandon Williams Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $2.63m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Is Brandon Williams’s Contract Worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Williams signed with Golden State on August 26, 2026, one year at the veteran minimum of $2.63m, with nothing guaranteed. A contract with no guarantee means the club owes him nothing if it waives him before the league’s January deadline. Signing in late August, after most rosters are settled, is how players in his position get their chance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Brandon Williams’s Net Worth in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Williams’s net worth is estimated at around $2m, worked back from about $4.90m in career earnings. No outlet publishes a figure for him. The real total is higher than that, because three of his five seasons were spent on two-way contracts and that compensation isn’t published. What can be said is that he’d earned under $2.32m in any single season before last year, and he went undrafted, so there was no rookie contract to start him off."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Do the Warriors Pay Brandon Williams $2.63m?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Williams is on a non-guaranteed minimum because he can score off the bench and hasn’t yet held a rotation place long enough for a club to commit. Surviving to January would give him the first fully paid season of his career."}}]}</script>
